I found no mitigation. withTenantConnection calls the instrumented pool.connect() before it enters any tenant scope. With RLS_ENFORCE=on, instrumentedConnect refuses a connect that has no AsyncLocalStorage scope. Nothing wraps the consolidation job in a scope at any level:
- the cron callback has none;
- runConsolidation has none;
- initMemoryConsolidationScheduler has none;
- registerProjectRoutes has none;
- registerPostStartRoutes, called from startServer, has none. The only system scope nearby, at index.ts:168, is a closed `.run()` around the RLS posture probe and does not leak into later code.

tenantStore uses `tenantStorage.run`, never enterWith, so no ambient scope can carry over into the cron timers. Other jobs avoid this failure by wrapping their work in runWithSystemTenantScope: scheduleOfEventsSweep, retentionCron, taskDueSweep, auditChainIntegritySweep, submission-chat-sweep-scheduler, and the pool.connect in run-control.ts:623. The consolidation job does not. The infrastructure-query exemption in enforcingScope takes a query text, and connect passes `undefined`, so the exemption cannot apply to connect. Production refuses to boot unless RLS_ENFORCE=on, and `on` is exactly the mode that trips the check. The last commit touching either file (906c94faf) is unrelated. docs/work-orders/README.md has no lane covering this.
